<span class="d-none" itemprop="commentCount">5</span>
	<div class="post-layout--right js-post-comments-component" data-has-opted-out="False">
        <div id="comments-80410" class="comments js-comments-container bt bc-black-200 mt12 " data-post-id="80410" data-min-length="15">
            <ul class="comments-list js-comments-list"
                    data-remaining-comments-count="0"
                    data-canpost="false"
                    data-cansee="true"
                    data-comments-unavailable="false"
                    data-addlink-disabled="true">

                    
    <li id="comment-206177" itemprop="comment" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" class="comment js-comment " data-comment-id="206177" data-comment-owner-id="18183" data-comment-score="0">
        <div class="js-comment-actions comment-actions">
            <div class="comment-score js-comment-score js-comment-edit-hide">
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="comment-text  js-comment-text-and-form">
            <div class="comment-body js-comment-edit-hide">
                <span class="d-none">$\begingroup$</span>
                <span class="comment-copy" itemprop="text">@Mattia: is this $M$ with the $\mathcal O_{X&#39;}$-structure you defined a line bundle on $X&#39;$? It should be given the above definition of deformation.</span>
                <span class="d-none">$\endgroup$</span>
                <div class="d-inline-flex ai-center" itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Person">
                    <div class="d-none" itemprop="name">Veen</div>
&ndash;&nbsp;
                        <a href="/users/18183/veen"
                           title="689 reputation"
                           class="comment-user owner"
                           itemprop="url">Veen</a>
                </div>
                <div class="d-none" itemprop="datePublished">2011-11-08 18:09:20 &#x2B;00:00</div>
                <span class="comment-date" dir="ltr">
                    <span class="v-visible-sr">Commented</span>
                    <span title='2011-11-08 18:09:20Z, License: CC BY-SA 3.0' class='relativetime-clean'>Nov 8, 2011 at 18:09</span>
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li id="comment-206235" itemprop="comment" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" class="comment js-comment " data-comment-id="206235" data-comment-owner-id="5516" data-comment-score="0">
        <div class="js-comment-actions comment-actions">
            <div class="comment-score js-comment-score js-comment-edit-hide">
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="comment-text  js-comment-text-and-form">
            <div class="comment-body js-comment-edit-hide">
                <span class="d-none">$\begingroup$</span>
                <span class="comment-copy" itemprop="text">I think so, if say $X$ is loc noetherian.  Take an open affine $U=Spec A \subseteq X$ (so the corresponding open of $X&#39;$ is the spectrum of $A&#39;=A[\varepsilon]$) and apply the local criterion of flatness for the nilpotent ideal $(\varepsilon)\subseteq A[\varepsilon]$ to the restriction of $M$ to $U$, call $N$ the corresponding $A&#39;$-module.  Namely, since $N/(\varepsilon N)$ is flat over $A$ (loc free even) and $Tor_1^{A&#39;}(N,A)=0$ (check that $\cdot \varepsilon: A\to A&#39;$ stays injective after tensoring with $N$), then $N$ is flat over $A&#39;$, so it is locally free.  (maybe there&#39;s an easier way..)</span>
                <span class="d-none">$\endgroup$</span>
                <div class="d-inline-flex ai-center" itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Person">
                    <div class="d-none" itemprop="name">Mattia Talpo</div>
&ndash;&nbsp;
                        <a href="/users/5516/mattia-talpo"
                           title="1,030 reputation"
                           class="comment-user"
                           itemprop="url">Mattia Talpo</a>
                </div>
                <div class="d-none" itemprop="datePublished">2011-11-08 20:27:28 &#x2B;00:00</div>
                <span class="comment-date" dir="ltr">
                    <span class="v-visible-sr">Commented</span>
                    <span title='2011-11-08 20:27:28Z, License: CC BY-SA 3.0' class='relativetime-clean'>Nov 8, 2011 at 20:27</span>
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li id="comment-206367" itemprop="comment" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" class="comment js-comment " data-comment-id="206367" data-comment-owner-id="18183" data-comment-score="0">
        <div class="js-comment-actions comment-actions">
            <div class="comment-score js-comment-score js-comment-edit-hide">
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="comment-text  js-comment-text-and-form">
            <div class="comment-body js-comment-edit-hide">
                <span class="d-none">$\begingroup$</span>
                <span class="comment-copy" itemprop="text">Well, but one needs locally free of rank one as one wants it to be a line bundle on $X&#39;$. But I think it really is, due to local splittings of the sequence $0\rightarrow L \rightarrow M \rightarrow L \rightarrow 0$ ($L$ is locally just the structure sheaf and so you get a retraction). Does this sound reasonable?</span>
                <span class="d-none">$\endgroup$</span>
                <div class="d-inline-flex ai-center" itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Person">
                    <div class="d-none" itemprop="name">Veen</div>
&ndash;&nbsp;
                        <a href="/users/18183/veen"
                           title="689 reputation"
                           class="comment-user owner"
                           itemprop="url">Veen</a>
                </div>
                <div class="d-none" itemprop="datePublished">2011-11-09 12:35:39 &#x2B;00:00</div>
                <span class="comment-date" dir="ltr">
                    <span class="v-visible-sr">Commented</span>
                    <span title='2011-11-09 12:35:39Z, License: CC BY-SA 3.0' class='relativetime-clean'>Nov 9, 2011 at 12:35</span>
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li id="comment-206374" itemprop="comment" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" class="comment js-comment " data-comment-id="206374" data-comment-owner-id="5516" data-comment-score="0">
        <div class="js-comment-actions comment-actions">
            <div class="comment-score js-comment-score js-comment-edit-hide">
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="comment-text  js-comment-text-and-form">
            <div class="comment-body js-comment-edit-hide">
                <span class="d-none">$\begingroup$</span>
                <span class="comment-copy" itemprop="text">Once you know that it is locally free, it must be of rank one, since its pullback to $X$ is..</span>
                <span class="d-none">$\endgroup$</span>
                <div class="d-inline-flex ai-center" itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Person">
                    <div class="d-none" itemprop="name">Mattia Talpo</div>
&ndash;&nbsp;
                        <a href="/users/5516/mattia-talpo"
                           title="1,030 reputation"
                           class="comment-user"
                           itemprop="url">Mattia Talpo</a>
                </div>
                <div class="d-none" itemprop="datePublished">2011-11-09 13:00:18 &#x2B;00:00</div>
                <span class="comment-date" dir="ltr">
                    <span class="v-visible-sr">Commented</span>
                    <span title='2011-11-09 13:00:18Z, License: CC BY-SA 3.0' class='relativetime-clean'>Nov 9, 2011 at 13:00</span>
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </li>
    <li id="comment-206639" itemprop="comment" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" class="comment js-comment " data-comment-id="206639" data-comment-owner-id="18183" data-comment-score="0">
